
Test Harness Overview
=====================

The scripts in this folder exercise the Teensy-based sniffer rig that proxies
RUN/RESET control lines and captures telemetry between the ClearCore (CC) and
Expansion Board (XPB). Use the unified CLI to drive each scenario:

	python test/rig_control.py --help

Common Options
--------------

* ``--port``: Serial port for the Teensy (auto-detected when possible).
* ``--baud``: USB CDC baud rate (default 460800).
* ``--no-drop-first-line``: Keep the first decoded frame (dropped by default to avoid startup noise).

COM target verification (required)
----------------------------------

Before any hardware run, confirm which serial port is the active sniffer. COM numbers can shift after
re-enumeration, USB hub changes, or power switching.

Example check:

```
python -c "from serial.tools import list_ports; [print(f'{p.device} | {p.description} | {p.hwid}') for p in list_ports.comports()]"
```

Use the detected sniffer COM port explicitly with ``--port`` for all test commands.

Available Modes
---------------

* ``reset-pulse``: Assert RESET low for a programmable duration and log the recovery.
* ``reset-pulse-multi``: Run multiple reset-pulse cycles back-to-back to stress-test SD/protocol reliability across reboots.
* ``run-pulse``: Toggle RUN low to start a drive cycle and capture CC/XBP heartbeats.
* ``reset-cancel``: Fire multiple sub-threshold RESET pulses to confirm cancel behavior.
* ``power --state on|off``: Toggle the sniffer-controlled board power relay for hard reset / cold boot validation.
* ``protocol-upload``: Walk through SD card staging, protocol ingestion, and automatic runtime validation. Adds preheat margin for heat protocols (``--preheat-s``, default 90 s).
* ``run-gate``: Automated five-step RUN-gate validation from CODE_REVIEW.md §7 — verifies boot masking, gate release, resume auto-start (RUN ON), manual-reset clears resume, and resume with RUN OFF (AUTOSTART=0).
* ``run-protocol``: (T9) Run a loaded protocol to completion and log RPM vs step. Reads the protocol CSV to auto-compute RUN pulse duration. When the protocol includes a ``TempC`` column with values > 0, a configurable preheat margin (``--preheat-s``, default 90 s) is added to the RUN hold.
* ``run-cycle``: (T2) Double-pulse RUN test — IDLE → RUNNING → PAUSED → RUNNING → PAUSED, with automated verdict.
* ``comms-health``: (T8) Passive comms health check — verify HB and STAT cadence stay within 2 s tolerance.
* ``cold-boot``: (T1) Power-cycle via sniffer relay, verify full boot sequence (QUIESCE → PROTO_RX=OK → IDLE HBs).
* ``heat-flags``: (T10) Two-phase heating validation — Phase A confirms no-heat protocol skips PREHEAT and heater stays OFF; Phase B (operator swaps SD to HEAT_TEST.csv) verifies PREHEAT entry, CMD;SP sent, and PID drives output. Interactive (requires SD swap).
* ``heat-lifecycle``: (T11) Four-phase heater lifecycle validation — Phase A: heater ON during RUNNING (PREHEAT + PID active); Phase B: heater OFF on PAUSED (CMD;SP=0 + OUT=000); Phase C: preheat on resume from pause (re-heat before motion); Phase D: heater OFF on COMPLETED (CMD;SP=0 + OUT=000). Requires heat protocol SD card already loaded (run T10 first or pre-load). Interactive.

Automated Test Suite
--------------------

``run_suite.py`` drives the individual ``rig_control.py`` verbs in sequence,
collects pass/fail verdicts, and prints a summary table.

Quick mode (default — no power-cycle tests):

```
python test/run_suite.py --port COM7
python test/run_suite.py --port COM7 --quick
```

Quick suite runs: T8 comms-health, T2 run-cycle, T5 reset-cancel.

Full mode (includes power-cycle and cold-boot):

```
python test/run_suite.py --port COM7 --full
```

Full suite adds: T4 reset-pulse, T6 reset-pulse-multi (×3), T1 cold-boot.

Manual Tests
------------

The following tests require operator observation and are not automated:

* **M1 — LCD inspection**: Verify home-screen layout: rows show STATE, TEMP,
  HEATER, STEP, and TIME values that update when running.
* **M2 — Soft reset transition**: Trigger a coordinated reset; confirm the LCD
  transitions directly to the Normal page (state, temp, step) without lingering
  on intermediate screens.
* **M3 — E-STOP recovery**: Disconnect/reconnect TTL cable while running; verify
  XPB detects E-STOP, CC receives CMD;PAUSE, and system pauses gracefully.
* **M4 — Heater PID**: Start a protocol with a temperature target; verify STAT;OUT
  values ramp up and stabilize near the setpoint over ~60 s.
  Semi-automated via ``heat-flags`` verb (T10): Phase A validates no-heat → heater OFF;
  Phase B validates heat protocol → PREHEAT + CMD;SP + PID output.  Use ``--auto`` to
  skip the interactive SD-swap prompt when the heat protocol SD is already inserted.
* **M5 — SD card removal**: Remove the SD card while idle; verify "Protocol Missing
  on SD" appears and the system rejects RUN attempts.
* **M6 — Motor movement**: (Deferred) Requires ClearCore motor docs review to
  design verification protocol.
* **M7 — Thermal alarm**: Verify over-temperature E-STOP fires when sump exceeds
  150 °C absolute ceiling or runs away > 35 °C above setpoint for 3 consecutive
  STAT frames. Cannot safely simulate on live hardware — verify via TTL injection
  or code inspection.

RUN-gate validation sequence
----------------------------

Validates the ClearCore RUN-gate firmware by running five sequential checks:

1. **Step 1:** Reset preamble (RESET pulse + power-cycle to clear stale SD resume), then cold-boot
   with RUN held low — CC must stay IDLE (gate masks the latched line).
2. **Step 2:** Release RUN, then re-assert — CC transitions IDLE→RUNNING→PAUSED.
3. **Step 3:** Create a resume snapshot during RUNNING, hard power-cut with RUN held ON — XPB sends
   ``CMD;RESUME=AUTO;AUTOSTART=1`` and CC accepts it, system enters RUNNING. Post-ACK verification
   only counts RUNNING/PREHEAT heartbeats after ``ACK;RESUME=OK``, then holds RUNNING for 15 s so
   the operator can visually confirm the LCD transition.
4. **Step 4:** Issue RESET pulse to clear resume state, cold-boot with RUN held — verify no
   ``CMD;RESUME=AUTO`` sent and system stays IDLE.
5. **Step 5:** Build new resume state, hard power-cut, cold-boot with RUN **OFF** — XPB sends
   ``CMD;RESUME=AUTO;AUTOSTART=0``, CC loads position but stays IDLE; then toggle RUN ON and
   verify system enters RUNNING from the resume point (not step 1).

Pass/fail is determined from observable TTL telemetry (``HB;STATE=``, ``CMD;RESUME=``,
``ACK;RESUME=``, ``NOTICE;PROTO_RX=OK``).  Use ``--skip-step-3`` for a quick steps 1-2 run.

Example:

```
python test/rig_control.py run-gate --port COM7
python test/rig_control.py run-gate --port COM7 --skip-step-3
python test/rig_control.py run-gate --port COM7 --boot-wait-s 40 --hb-window-s 15
```

Hard reset sequence (power cycle)
---------------------------------

Use the power mode to perform a true board hard reset and capture boot traffic:

```
python test/rig_control.py power --state off --capture-s 4
python test/rig_control.py power --state on --capture-s 8 --drop-first-line
```

Reset-pulse stress test
-----------------------

Run multiple consecutive reset-pulse cycles to check whether protocol reload from
SD survives repeated soft-resets:

```
python test/rig_control.py reset-pulse-multi --port COM7
python test/rig_control.py reset-pulse-multi --port COM7 --count 10
python test/rig_control.py reset-pulse-multi --port COM7 --count 3 --boot-wait-s 40
```

Summary is printed at the end with pass/fail per iteration. Each iteration checks
for ``NOTICE;PROTO_RX=OK`` or ``HB;STATE=IDLE`` as evidence of successful protocol
reload.

For complete project resume context, see [docs/PROJECT_HANDOFF.md](../docs/PROJECT_HANDOFF.md)
and [CODE_REVIEW.md](../CODE_REVIEW.md).

Legacy entry points such as ``reset_pulse_test.py`` now forward to the CLI above,
so existing shortcuts continue to work while new scenarios can be added as
additional subcommands.
